---
source: crates/lobo-cli/tests/help_parity.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(output).unwrap()"
---
Rent a 5090 and boot lobo; shows progress until the API is ready

Usage:
  lobo up [OPTIONS]

Flags:
      --cloud <string>       community ($0.69/h, default, community hosts only) or secure (datacenter $0.99/h first, community fallback) [default: community]
      --conns <int>          parallel download streams on the pod (0 = agent default)
      --ctx <int>            context size (0 = release default)
      --idle-min <int>       minutes without requests before the pod deletes itself (0 = release default)
      --image <string>       pod image with lobo-agent baked in, e.g. ghcr.io/1905/lobocode@sha256:… (default: LOBO_POD_IMAGE, else the release zip)
      --json[=<JSON>]        one JSON object per event on stdout (for scripts and tests)
      --max-life <duration>  hard pod lifetime, e.g. 12h (0 = release default)
      --min-mbps <int>       drop the pod if the model downloads slower than this after 20 s (0 = LOBO_MIN_MBPS or 100)
      --plain[=<PLAIN>]      log lines instead of the TUI
      --provider <string>    runpod, vast or local (this Mac) (default: LOBO_PROVIDER, else the one with a key, runpod first)
      --q6[=<Q6>]            serve Q6_K instead of the release default
      --release <string>     release version (default latest)
      --source <string>      model source: r2 (presigned, default) | feesh (the model server HTTP) | ssh (the model server SSH) | public (r2.dev)
      --ssh <string>         debug: path to a public key; opens 22/tcp and runs sshd on the pod
  -h, --help                 help for up

Global Flags:
      --config <string>  config file (dotenv; the OS env is never read) [default: /home/u/.config/lobo/config.env]
